{"id": "1cd2e5c3-2f57-4c3a-a161-d9ad01b6711a", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I should be upfront that I haven't actually inspected their environment, so I'll frame this as a prioritized starting point rather than a definitive diagnosis, and offer to verify things like evaluation jobs or metric filters in a read-only way before suggesting changes.

For substance: lock prompts behind PR-only deploys, build a versioned golden eval dataset with a baseline score, run automated CI evals gating promotion on a workload-specific margin (accounting for judge variance), restrict deploy permissions to the pipeline with reviewer approval, and add a production backstop—logging, a stopReason alarm, and rollback capability. I'll flag that automated metrics aren't sufficient proof for high-stakes cases and that I can't verify their actual CI/CD wiring, then decide what's essential now versus what can wait.

